This project is a python representation of a library system.

At the start of the program, if there was an existing list of books in the library it is loaded into the list variable "Library". The user is then given a menu to choose from. They enter the numbers corresponding to the menu option they wish for.

If the user enters "1" the AddBook function is run. The function allows new book entries with their corresponding authors while preventing duplicate entries. The struggles I experienced with this section were brainstorming all possible conditions that would affect whether or not a book was added.

If the user enters "2" or "3" the StatusChange function is run. The user then inputs the book they want to borrow/return. Depending on their response, the specified book's status changes (Available/Borrowed). There were no major struggles in this area.


If the user enters a a value that isn't a number or a number not in the range of 1-7, it triggers a ValueError; an error message is output and they are asked to choose again.

And finally, if the user enters "7" the program ends